
rchitectural summary of all the key decisions:
Hybrid text analysis architecture: Instead of relying on rigid, rule-based filters or error-prone string length checks, we introduced a dedicated ignore class in the training dataset to let the machine learning model intelligently filter out greetings, signatures, and noise.
Confidence thresholding for risk mitigation: To prevent the model from blindly guessing ambiguous text, we implemented a confidence threshold ($\ge 60\%$) that safely routes low-certainty predictions directly to an administrator (admin), protecting the system from false positives.
Sentence-level parsing for compound intents: Emails are split into individual sentences via punctuation marks and newlines, allowing the pipeline to correctly catch multiple distinct actions within a single multi-intent email (e.g., booking a court while simultaneously asking a question).
Estonian morphology via EstNLTK: Before vectorization, incoming text is preprocessed using EstNLTK's morphological analyzer, stripping punctuation and reducing all words to their base lemmas (.isalpha()), which ensures robust recognition regardless of grammatical cases (väljakut, väljakul -> väljak).
Bigram context capture (ngram_range): The TfidfVectorizer was configured with bigrams to preserve short word pairs (such as "ei soovi"), empowering the model to accurately capture negations and contextual nuances.
Strict decoupling of NLP and backend logic: The mathematics and classification logic (train_model.py and nlp_parser.py) are completely isolated from the FastAPI service, with the parser returning a clean set of recognized intents without any direct database dependencies.
Resilient IMAP email reading: The email reader wrapper incorporates robust error handling, multipart payload traversal, and UTF-8 decoding with errors="ignore", guaranteeing that malformed or non-standard client encodings will never crash the core FastAPI server.
Clean and intuitive FastAPI routing: Business logic is organized into clean conditional flows in main.py, ensuring that bookings trigger time extraction and database checks, while ambiguities or inquiries are seamlessly delegated to human administrators.


